<aiml version="1.0">
<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS TERM BLUE BOX AND HOW DID IT ORIGINATE</pattern>
<template>The term 'blue box' is a colloquial term that originated from folklore about early phone phreaking boxes. It refers to electronic devices used to bypass telephone network authentication and make long-distance calls without paying. John Draper created the first blue box in the 1960s, establishing the foundation for the hobby. These devices were sold door-to-door by groups like 'Berkeley Blue' and 'Oaf Tobar' in the 1970s.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS FIRST KNOWN USE OF BLUE BOXES IN TELEPHONE NETWORK</pattern>
<template>Blue boxes were first used in the 1960s to manipulate long-distance call routing and billing systems.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS PURPOSE OF BLUE BOXES IN 1980S</pattern>
<template>By the 1980s, the transition to digital signaling rendered audio-based blue boxes obsolete, ending their practical use.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS NAME OF BLUE BOX SUBCULTURE</pattern>
<template>The blue box subculture emerged from early telephone network exploitation and was popularized by Apple co-founders Steve Wozniak and Steve Jobs.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WERE DIFFERENT COLORED BOXES DEVELOPED FOR PHONE NETWORK</pattern>
<template>Multiple colored boxes were developed (blue, red, silver, magenta, orange, vermilion, etc.) to control different aspects of the phone network.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS TECHNICAL MECHANISM USED BY EARLY BLUE BOXES</pattern>
<template>Early blue boxes used simple tone generation.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS TECHNICAL MECHANISM USED BY LATER BLUE BOXES</pattern>
<template>Later versions incorporated complex systems like System 4 for international circuits.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WAS LIFESPAN OF BLUE BOXES IN TELEPHONE NETWORK</pattern>
<template>Blue boxes were primarily associated with long-distance toll fraud, but similar "color boxes" were also developed to control other network functions beyond just long-distance calling.</template>
</category>
<category>
<pattern>WHAT WERE SOURCES USED TO COMPILE THIS REPORT</pattern>
<template>The report was compiled from Wikipedia articles on blue boxes and phreaking, as well as related sources from Internet Pasaasoapaso and PhilTel.</template>
</category>
</aiml>
